# GitHub Code Analyzer — Claude Plugin

[![CI](https://github.com/your-username/github-code-analyzer/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/your-username/github-code-analyzer/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
[![Coverage](https://codecov.io/gh/your-username/github-code-analyzer/branch/main/graph/badge.svg)](https://codecov.io/gh/your-username/github-code-analyzer)
[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.11%20%7C%203.12-blue)](https://www.python.org)
[![MCP](https://img.shields.io/badge/protocol-MCP-purple)](https://modelcontextprotocol.io)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](LICENSE)

Scan any public (or private, with a token) GitHub repository and instantly generate six types of technical diagram:

| Diagram | What it shows |
|---------|--------------|
| **Architecture** | Layered topology: client → API → services → database → infra |
| **Data Flow** | Request lifecycle, auth steps, cache branches, async queues |
| **ER Diagram** | ORM entities and foreign-key relationships |
| **Sequence** | Actor interactions across a numbered request/response cycle |
| **Component Map** | Module-level import dependency graph |
| **Deployment** | Container, IaC, and CI/CD infrastructure topology |

All output is [Mermaid](https://mermaid.js.org/) rendered inline in Claude.

---

## Quick start

### 1. Install

```bash
# From the published plugin directory
claude plugin install github-code-analyzer

# Or from a local clone
git clone https://github.com/your-username/github-code-analyzer
claude plugin install ./github-code-analyzer
```

### 2. (Recommended) Add a GitHub token

Without a token you are limited to **60 unauthenticated GitHub API requests / hour**.
With a token the limit rises to **5,000 / hour**.

```bash
# https://github.com/settings/tokens → New token → read:repo scope
export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

Or set it permanently in `~/.claude/settings.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github-code-analyzer": {
      "env": { "GITHUB_TOKEN": "ghp_xxx" }
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. Ask Claude

```
Analyse the architecture of https://github.com/vercel/next.js
```
```
Generate an ER diagram for github.com/prisma/prisma
```
```
Show me the data flow for django/django
```
```
Map out the component dependencies in fastapi/fastapi
```

---

## Tools reference

| Tool | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `analyze_repository` | Run all 6 diagrams + overview in a single call |
| `generate_architecture_diagram` | Layered system architecture (Mermaid `graph TB`) |
| `generate_data_flow_diagram` | Request lifecycle with auth, cache, and queue paths |
| `generate_er_diagram` | Entity-Relationship from ORM model definitions |
| `generate_sequence_diagram` | Numbered actor sequence with cache hit/miss branches |
| `generate_component_diagram` | Import-based module dependency graph |
| `generate_deployment_diagram` | Container, IaC, and CI/CD infra topology |
| `get_repo_overview` | Plain-text structural summary (file counts, routes, models, …) |

### Optional parameters

`analyze_repository` accepts a `max_files` parameter (default `80`, max `300`) to
control how many source files are read for deep analysis:

```
Analyse fastapi/fastapi with max_files=200
```

