## Supported technologies

### Frameworks (auto-detected)

React · Next.js · Nuxt.js · Vue · SvelteKit · Django · FastAPI / Flask ·
Rails · Spring Boot · Laravel · Express · NestJS

### ORM / Schema (for ER diagrams)

Django ORM · SQLAlchemy · Prisma · TypeORM · Sequelize · ActiveRecord · Mongoose

### Infrastructure

Docker · Docker Compose · Kubernetes · Helm · Terraform ·
GitHub Actions · GitLab CI · CircleCI · Nginx

### External services (detected in architecture / deployment)

Auth / JWT · Redis / Cache · Message Queues (Celery, RabbitMQ, Kafka, Sidekiq) ·
Email (SendGrid, SES, Mailgun) · Storage (S3, GCS, Cloudinary) ·
Search (Elasticsearch, Algolia) · Payments (Stripe, PayPal) ·
Monitoring (Sentry, Datadog, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry)

### Languages (source analysis)

Python · TypeScript · JavaScript · Go · Java · Ruby · Rust · C# · PHP · Kotlin

---

## Security

- **No raw file content in responses.** Source files are consumed by the
  analyser and converted to structured data (model names, route paths, import
  graphs). Only synthesised Mermaid diagrams are returned, preventing
  prompt-injection attacks embedded in repository source.
- **Strict input validation.** Repo identifiers are validated against GitHub's
  naming rules before any network request is made.
- **Token never logged.** `GITHUB_TOKEN` is read from the environment only and
  is never included in tool output or server logs.

See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) for the full security policy and responsible
disclosure process.

---

## Requirements

- Python 3.11 or 3.12
- Dependencies: `mcp>=1.0.0`, `httpx>=0.27.0`

```bash
pip install -r server/requirements.txt
# or
pip install -e .
```

---

## Development

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/github-code-analyzer
cd github-code-analyzer
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run tests (≥ 80% coverage required)
pytest

# Lint + format + type-check
ruff check server/ tests/
ruff format server/ tests/
mypy server/
```

See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) for the full guide.

